  "system": {
    "name": "arcade-test",
    "summary": "A step-by-step walkthrough of Arcade.dev, in which Python scripts and Claude act on a user's GitHub account through Arcade. Claude chooses the tools and writes their arguments, and Arcade runs each one as that user after a one-time GitHub sign-in. Custom tools in my_server are deployed to Arcade Cloud, and Claude Code can use the same tools through an MCP Gateway. Step 8 adds per-user conversation memory in Redis, running in Docker on your machine.",
    "highlights": [
      "OAuth tokens never leave Arcade: neither this code nor Claude ever sees one.",
      "Arcade stores every sign-in against a `user_id`, so one user can't borrow another's GitHub access.",
      "The code holds just two API keys, read from `.env`: one for Arcade and one for Anthropic.",
      "Redis has no password, so `compose.yaml` binds it to 127.0.0.1 only.",
      "The project's own GitHub App (`kenkyl-github`) overrides Arcade's default, so every GitHub tool signs in through it."
    ]
  },
